326	/**
327	 * The figures of one person's claims, as the screen works them out: a settled claim's frozen due, else the
328	 * figure its person's last statement bound it to (not while PENDING), else its live due (amount times the rate in force on its date of
329	 * the grade its person had on its date, rounded by the sheet's policy, and at least the sheet's floor; none — n/a — when no rate applies then). An
330	 * overdue claim's due adds, on top of its figure, the late charge: the sheet's late percent of the figure for every
331	 * full 30 days it is overdue on the sheet's today, rounded like a due. A statement never binds the charge; settling
332	 * freezes it in. A correction's live due is its amount times the rate, rounded the same way, with no floor, and it
333	 * never takes a late charge. The rounding policy: a claim dated before the sheet's policy date (its today when blank)
334	 * rounds half up, one dated on or after it half to even; a correction goes by the date of the claim it corrects.
